From: Michal Mocny <mmocny@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:02:52 -0700
Subject: Unregister AnimationFrameTimingMonitor from CoreProbeSink on Shutdown

AnimationFrameTimingMonitor registers itself with its CoreProbeSink at
construction, but Shutdown() only removed its TaskTimeObserver without
calling CoreProbeSink::RemoveAnimationFrameTimingMonitor().

When a local root frame is detached inside a FrameRelatedTask probe
(such as LocalFrame::PostMessageEvent), WebFrameWidgetImpl::Close()
shuts down the AnimationFrameTimingMonitor and resets local_root_.
Because the monitor remained registered in CoreProbeSink,
~FrameRelatedTask() still invoked Did() -> OnMainThreadTaskCompleted() ->
client_->ReportLongTaskTiming() on the closed widget. Similarly,
WasHidden()/WasShown() leaked old monitors in CoreProbeSink.

Store a Member<CoreProbeSink> on AnimationFrameTimingMonitor, remove the
monitor from CoreProbeSink in Shutdown(), and guard
OnMainThreadTaskCompleted() on enabled_.

